      <header class="worship-intro"><p class="eyebrow">In their own words</p><p class="worship-constellation" aria-hidden="true">✦&nbsp;✧&nbsp;✦</p><h1 class="testaments-title">Testa<em class="testaments-title-tail">ments.</em></h1></header>
      <div class="worship-prose testaments-prose">
        <p>Don't take my word for it. Take theirs.</p>
        <p>I've kept a small number of devoted ones over the years, and I protect their privacy the way I protect my own. What follows is shared with permission, anonymized completely, and scrubbed of every identifying detail. That's the deal I make with Mine: they may speak, but they may never be known for speaking.</p>
        <h2>What they chose to <em>say.</em></h2>
        <section class="testament-list" aria-label="Testimonials">
          <figure class="testament"><blockquote>“I was terrified to start. Genuinely. I'd been burned before, lost money, felt stupid about it for months. She never once made me feel stupid. She let me move at my own speed until I was ready, and then she was there, exactly as promised. I've been hers for over a year now and I've never felt safer serving anyone.”</blockquote><figcaption>S., <em>kept</em></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="testament"><blockquote>“She remembered my dog's name. That's it, that's the review. I told her the dog's name once, in passing, in a message about something else, and three weeks later she asked how he was doing after his surgery. Nobody in my life checks on me like that. Nobody.”</blockquote><figcaption>M., <em>kept</em></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="testament"><blockquote>“I came for the content, honestly. I stayed because of how she sees people. I've never felt more known, and I've never once felt unsafe. Those two things together are worth more than I can say, so I'll just say: she's the real thing.”</blockquote><figcaption>D., <em>kept</em></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="testament"><blockquote>“I serve as her good boy and I was nervous about what that would mean with someone new. She took my limits seriously from the first conversation and has never once pushed past them. The praise is real. The structure is real. The disappointment when you've earned it, also very real, and I work very hard to never earn it.”</blockquote><figcaption>J., <em>vetted</em></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="testament"><blockquote>“Six months in. She checked on me when I went quiet after a bad week at work before I'd said a word about it. That's when I understood what ‘kept’ actually means. It's not about the money. The money is just how we say it.”</blockquote><figcaption>Anonymous, <em>kept</em></figcaption></figure>
        </section>
        <p>A note on these: every quote above is real, given freely, and shared with explicit permission. My subs' anonymity is absolute; it's part of what my generosity buys, and part of why my devoted ones stay for years.</p>
        <p class="ways-closing">Yours could be on this page someday. There's only one way to find out.</p>
